<section class="specialized-notes privacy-seo-compact" aria-labelledby="privacy-notes-title">
  <header><span class="section-index">AFTER THE CHECK</span><h2 id="privacy-notes-title">Three things worth knowing</h2><p>The score points to stored clues. It is not a promise that an image is anonymous.</p></header>
  <div class="specialized-note-list">
    <details>
      <summary>What metadata can reveal</summary>
      <div><p>GPS can identify a place. Device serial numbers, names, contact fields, original filenames, timestamps, thumbnails, editing IDs, and AI workflows can connect an image to a person, device, or project.</p></div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>How the score works</summary>
      <div><p>The 0–100 score uses visible, capped rules. Exact coordinates matter more than a camera model, and repeated copies of the same fact do not earn the same points twice.</p></div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>What the checker cannot see</summary>
      <div><p>It does not analyze faces, signs, addresses, plates, reflections, screens, uniforms, or landmarks in the pixels. Removing metadata cannot hide visible details.</p><a class="inline-link" href="/metadata-remover">Create and verify a cleaned copy</a></div>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>
